# Task 9 — Password-Protected ZIP Files

John cannot directly treat a ZIP archive as a normal hash file.

First, convert the ZIP file into a John-readable format using:

```text
zip2john
```

## Convert ZIP

```bash
zip2john secure.zip > zip_hash.txt
```

This creates:

```text
zip_hash.txt
```

## Crack

```bash
john --wordlist=/usr/share/wordlists/rockyou.txt zip_hash.txt
```

## Show Password

```bash
john --show zip_hash.txt
```

## Extract ZIP

After obtaining the password:

```bash
unzip secure.zip
```

To list its contents without extracting:

```bash
unzip -l secure.zip
```

---

# Task 10 — Password-Protected RAR Files

RAR is a compressed archive format commonly associated with WinRAR.

Use:

```text
rar2john
```

to convert the archive into a John-readable format.

## Convert RAR

```bash
rar2john secure.rar > rar_hash.txt
```

On the AttackBox, it may also be available as:

```bash
/opt/john/rar2john secure.rar > rar_hash.txt
```

## Crack

```bash
john --wordlist=/usr/share/wordlists/rockyou.txt rar_hash.txt
```

## Extract

After obtaining the password:

```bash
unrar x secure.rar
```

