# Task 11 — SSH Private-Key Passwords

SSH private keys such as:

```text
id_rsa
```

can be protected with a password/passphrase.

John can test passwords against the protection applied to the private key.

## Convert with `ssh2john`

```bash
ssh2john id_rsa > id_rsa_hash.txt
```

If the command is unavailable, the AttackBox may use:

```bash
python3 /opt/john/ssh2john.py id_rsa > id_rsa_hash.txt
```

Kali may use:

```bash
python /usr/share/john/ssh2john.py id_rsa > id_rsa_hash.txt
```

## Crack

```bash
john --wordlist=/usr/share/wordlists/rockyou.txt id_rsa_hash.txt
```

## Show Result

```bash
john --show id_rsa_hash.txt
```

